\begin{small}
\begin{verbatim}
{"type": "object",
 "properties": {
   "relation": {"type": "string",
     "enum": [<sorted_types>, "none"]}},
 "required": ["relation"]}
\end{verbatim}
\end{small}

\subsection{Type Definitions}
\label{sec:appendix_type_defs}

All prompts include per-type natural-language definitions sourced from the respective dataset documentation:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*,itemsep=2pt]
\item \textbf{Few-NERD:} 66 fine-grained entity types with definitions derived from the Few-NERD type ontology \cite{fewnerd-2021}.
\item \textbf{MAVEN:} 168 event types with FrameNet-based definitions \cite{maven-2020}.
\item \textbf{FewRel:} 80 relation types with Wikidata property descriptions \cite{fewrel-2018}.
